type: software
title: "WordBuddy: Cognitive Interactions with Robots for Educational Purposes"
abstract: >
  WordBuddy is an interactive educational robotic system that helps children
  improve English word recognition and spelling through physical interaction
  with letter blocks. The system integrates a UR3 collaborative robot arm,
  a CNN-based computer vision pipeline for letter recognition, and an adaptive
  game logic engine with three game modes (Spelling Bee, Fill the Gap, Find the
  Error). It uses text-to-speech feedback to create an engaging human-robot
  interaction learning environment.
